-- title:
--   Place over an Igusa component reads the supersingular place s
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5\le q$ and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $k=\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ and $\mathrm{res}_A\colon A\to k$ for the residue map. Two function fields inside Laurent series are in play: $\mathcal F(M')=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$, and $\mathcal F_H=\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'=\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; the hypothesis `hle` asserts $\mathcal F(M')\le\mathcal F_H$. On the reduced side, $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,M'$ is the $k$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k)$ generated by `jqModC k` and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion, and $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}\,k\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ is the $k$-subfield generated by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$; places are always [`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22), that is, valuation subrings of the ambient field containing the base field, proper, and principal ideal rings, with $\mathrm{ord}$, $\mathrm{evalAt}$ and rationality as defined there.
--
--   The finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,M'$ over $k$ is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the supersingular places in the sense of `ssPlaces`: those $w$ which are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace k M'`, and for which $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen k M'` lies in `ssJSet q k`. The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathcal F(M')$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathcal F(M')$, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the reduced field with kernel the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisor pushforward, together with the conditions that $\mathrm{algebraMap}$ of $x\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when $x\in A$, that $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ agrees with $\mathrm{res}_A$ on constants, and that every nonzero $f$ can be scaled into the integers with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` fixes $R_0$ coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ lies in $\mathcal F(M')$, that element belongs to $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $k$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Moreover $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$, and $\zeta$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an element of $\mathrm{Idx}\,q$).
--
--   Two families of valuation subrings of $\mathcal F_H$ are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)=\mathrm{CuspidalType.ProjLine}\,q$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. The Igusa group of hypotheses reads: `hIg_inf` describes the ring at the line $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q=[1:0]$, namely $f\in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot\iota(y)=\iota(x)$, where $\iota$ is the coefficientwise map induced by $A\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg` asserts that every line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma\cdot\infty$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ (reduction of $\gamma$ modulo $q$ acting on $\mathbb P^1$) with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under the automorphism $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ of $\mathcal F_H$ attached to $\zeta$ and $\gamma$; `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm` asserts that for every primitive root $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the preimages along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ permute the family, i.e. are of the form $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma\ell)$ for a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$.
--
--   The supersingular group reads: `hSS_A` asserts that for each $s\in W$ a constant $x\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has its image in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when $x\in A$; `hSS_over` asserts that for $s\in W$ and $f\in\mathcal F(M')$ lying in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of $\mathcal F(M')$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the coefficientwise image $\hat\jmath$ of `jq` has nonnegative order, and such that $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F_H$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$, the difference of that image and the constant $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in fact in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix` asserts that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own preimage under every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr` provides for each $s\in W$ an element $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t$ minus any constant $a\in A$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   The descent data are: a subfield $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over $K_0$ and $\pi\in K_0$; a Henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota\colon A_0\to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A\cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`) and for which $\mathrm{res}_A\circ\iota$ is surjective (`hres`); a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ with $\iota(\varpi_0)=\pi$; a subfield $F_0\subseteq\mathcal F_H$ characterised by `hF₀` as the set of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$; the hypothesis `hjF₀` that the image of $\hat\jmath$ under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $F_0$, this element (nonzero) being the $\hat\jmath$ used below; and an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ which by `hj₀` sends $a\in A_0$ to the constant $\iota(a)$ of $\mathcal F_H$.
--
--   Finally, $s\in W$ and $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ are fixed, and $O_\ell$ denotes the valuation subring $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)\cap F_0$ of $F_0$, that is, the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ under the inclusion of $F_0$. Write $E=\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}\,k\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$. The data are a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from the residue field of $O_\ell$ to $E$ and a ring endomorphism $\tau$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k)$ which by `hτ` is either the identity or the substitution $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k\,(q^2)$. The compatibilities required of $\rho$ are: `hρA`, that on constants $\rho$ of the residue of $\mathrm{algebraMap}(a)$, for $a\in A_0$ with $\mathrm{algebraMap}(a)\in O_\ell$, is the image in $E$ of $\mathrm{res}_A(\iota a)$; and `hρf`, that for $f\in\mathcal F(M')$ lying in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, for $a\in A_0$ and for $g$ in $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,F_0\,\hat\jmath$ — the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $F_0$ integral over $A_0[\hat\jmath]$ — with $g\in O_\ell$, whenever $g$ equals the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F_H$ minus the constant $\iota(a)$, the Laurent series of $\rho$ of the residue of $g$ equals $\tau$ applied to the Laurent series of $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ minus the constant $\mathrm{res}_A(\iota a)$.
--
--   The place $w$ of $E$ over $k$ is subject to two reading hypotheses. By `hwC`, for every $g$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,F_0\,\hat\jmath$ with $g\in O_\ell$, the element $\rho$ of the residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $w$. By `hread`, for every $f\in\mathcal F(M')$ lying in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which has nonnegative order at every place of $\mathcal F(M')$ where $\hat\jmath$ does and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, for every $a\in A_0$ with $\mathrm{res}_A(\iota a)=s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$, and for every $g$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,F_0\,\hat\jmath$ with $g\in O_\ell$ equal to the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F_H$ minus the constant $\iota(a)$, the element $\rho$ of the residue of $g$ lies in the non-units of the valuation subring of $w$.
--
--   Under all of these hypotheses, for any $g\in\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,M'$ and $g'\in E$ whose Laurent series satisfy $g'=\tau(g)$, the conclusion is the equivalence
--   $$g\in s.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}\iff g'\in w.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}.$$
--
--   This is the step in which a place $w$ of the reduced level-$H$ function field, specified by the residues of the integral chart functions on an Igusa component $\ell$ and by the vanishing of the reductions of traces of floor functions, is shown to lie over the supersingular place $s$ of the reduced level-$M'$ function field: membership in the valuation ring of $s$ is read off, through the substitution $\tau$, from membership in the valuation ring of $w$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_valuationSubring_residueField_igusaRing_of_floorTrace_descent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_valuationSubring_residueField_igusaRing_of_floorTrace_descent) in the analysis of the reduction of the full-level modular curve at $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_forall_mem_iff_mem_of_place_reads_ssPlace_igusaRing_descent.lean

